  "Notes": [
    "Self-contained input. Every pressure is absolute Pa; velocities are interstitial at the specified source pressure and temperature.",
    "Adsorption feed and cold HTF reference are 298.15 K; nonisothermal bed temperatures are solved.",
    "Original two-site fit order and full workbook precision are retained; no mixture refit. SEI is not SCI or IAST.",
    "Kinetics, transport, pellet density and hardware are common screening assumptions, not measured material properties.",
    "The energy equation uses the 298.15 K Henry-limit-weighted constant heat from the supplied site fits; equilibrium retains both individual site heats.",
    "Light purge uses remembered product composition and is subtracted from net product. Pure-CH4 fallback is startup only; a finite product tank is not modelled.",
    "Two-column CSS compares a complete schedule with both A/B role exchanges; total adsorbent mass is used for productivity.",
